#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:3
msgid "Building the Documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:5
msgid ""
"This page explains how to build the LLVM-libc HTML documentation locally so "
"you can preview changes before submitting a patch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:8
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:10
msgid ""
"The LLVM documentation build uses [Sphinx](https://www.sphinx-doc.org/). The "
"key packages required are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:13
msgid "`sphinx` — the documentation generator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:14
msgid "`furo` — the theme used by LLVM-libc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:15
msgid "`myst-parser` — Markdown support alongside RST"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:16
msgid "`sphinx-reredirects` — handles page redirect entries in `conf.py`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:18
msgid "**On Debian/Ubuntu**, all required packages are available via apt:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:25
msgid ""
"**On other systems**, install everything from the shared requirements file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:31
msgid "CMake Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:33
msgid ""
"Enable the Sphinx documentation build by adding these flags to your CMake "
"invocation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:44
msgid ""
"The `LLVM_ENABLE_SPHINX=ON` flag enables Sphinx globally for all LLVM "
"subprojects. `LIBC_INCLUDE_DOCS=ON` is specific to libc and tells CMake to "
"register the libc doc targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:48
msgid "Building"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:50
msgid "Once configured, build the HTML docs with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:56
msgid ""
"The output is written to `<build-dir>/tools/libc/docs/html/`. Open "
"`index.html` in a browser to view the site."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:59
msgid "Header Status Pages (Auto-generated)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:61
msgid ""
"The per-header implementation status pages under `docs/headers/` are **not** "
"hand-written RST. They are generated at build time by `libc/utils/docgen/"
"docgen.py`, which:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:65
msgid "Reads YAML function definitions from `libc/src/<header>/*.yaml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:66
msgid "Scans `libc/src/<header>/` for `.cpp` implementation files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:67
msgid "Checks `libc/include/llvm-libc-macros/` for macro `#define` entries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:68
msgid ""
"Emits an RST `list-table` showing each symbol's implementation status, C "
"standard section, and POSIX link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:71
msgid ""
"If you add a new function and regenerate, these pages update automatically. "
"Do **not** hand-edit the generated RST files in `docs/headers/` — your "
"changes will be overwritten the next time the docs are built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:75
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:77
msgid "`Extension error: Could not import extension myst_parser`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:78
msgid ""
"On Debian/Ubuntu: `sudo apt-get install python3-myst-parser`. Otherwise: "
"`pip install -r llvm/docs/requirements.txt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:81
msgid "`WARNING: document isn't included in any toctree`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:82
msgid ""
"A new RST/Markdown file needs a `toctree` entry. Add it to the appropriate "
"`index.rst` or its parent toctree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:85
msgid "`Extension error: No module named 'sphinx_reredirects'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building_docs.md:86
msgid "Same fix: `pip install -r llvm/docs/requirements.txt`."
msgstr ""
